  "financing": {
   "name": "Construction and permanent financing norms (US, Oct 2026)",
   "file": "_common/financing.json",
   "items": {
    "constructionLoanRate": {
     "id": "constructionLoanRate",
     "name": "Construction loan all-in interest rate (floating, 2026)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Floating rate. Rate caps or floors and SOFR moves over an 18-30 month draw period can shift the realized rate by +/-50-100 bp.",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.064,
      "mid": 0.07,
      "high": 0.085,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [
        "_common/financing.json#e1",
        "_common/financing.json#e2",
        "_common/financing.json#e3",
        "_common/financing.json#e4",
        "_common/financing.json#e6"
       ],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "All-in = 1-month SOFR (about 3.89%: e1, e2) + lender spread. No public, current survey of construction-loan spreads was found, so the spreads are an assumption: bank/regional-bank construction ~SOFR+2.50 to +3.50 (often quoted as prime, e3, = SOFR+3.1); debt-fund/non-bank ~SOFR+4.0 to +5.0. Low = 3.89+2.50 = 6.4%. Mid = prime, 7.00% (3.89+3.11). High = 3.89+4.60 = about 8.5% (non-bank, higher leverage). Tight CLD standards (e6) argue against the low end for spec projects. Verify spreads with a lender quote."
      }
     }
    },
    "loanToCost": {
     "id": "loanToCost",
     "name": "Construction loan-to-cost (LTC)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Equity first: the loan funds only after the (1 - LTC) equity is spent, as the engine models.",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.5,
      "mid": 0.6,
      "high": 0.7,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [
        "_common/financing.json#e5",
        "_common/financing.json#e6"
       ],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "Regulatory loan-to-value ceilings (e5): 80% for commercial/multifamily construction, 85% for 1-4 family. Lenders size well inside these and usually also cap LTC. With CLD standards at the tighter end of their range (e6), bank senior construction loans are assumed at 50-65% LTC and up to 70-75% with recourse, strong sponsors or non-bank lenders. Mid 60%. Agency/HUD 221(d)(4) programs go higher, but no source page could be retrieved this session (not cited)."
      }
     }
    },
    "constructionLoanFee": {
     "id": "constructionLoanFee",
     "name": "Construction loan origination fee (% of loan commitment)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Applied to the loan commitment at close.",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.005,
      "mid": 0.01,
      "high": 0.015,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "Industry convention of 0.5-1.5 points (1 point = 1% of commitment), paid at closing; mid 1.0 point. No public survey was retrievable this session. Excludes lender legal, inspection and title (budget those as soft costs) and any exit fee (0-1%) charged by non-bank lenders."
      }
     }
    },
    "averageOutstandingBalance": {
     "id": "averageOutstandingBalance",
     "name": "Average outstanding balance as share of loan commitment (construction + lease-up carry)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Shortcut check only: interest = loan x rate x (construction + lease-up months)/12 x this factor. The engine itself simulates monthly draws.",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.5,
      "mid": 0.6,
      "high": 0.7,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "Monthly simulation (scratch model): 20% of cost up front (land/soft), remaining hard cost on an S-curve (smoothstep), equity first, then loan draws, then the loan held fully drawn through lease-up until takeout. Average balance / commitment over construction + lease-up: 18-mo build + 6-mo lease-up = 0.54-0.59 (LTC 55-70%); 18 + 12 = 0.63-0.67; 24 + 6 = 0.50-0.56; 24 + 12 = 0.59-0.63; 12 + 12 = 0.69-0.72. Range 0.50-0.70, mid 0.60. Matches the common 55-65% rule of thumb when interest is figured over construction + lease-up."
      }
     }
    },
    "averageOutstandingBalanceConstructionOnly": {
     "id": "averageOutstandingBalanceConstructionOnly",
     "name": "Average outstanding balance, construction period only (equity first)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Use when the shortcut covers construction months only.",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.38,
      "mid": 0.42,
      "high": 0.45,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "Same simulation, averaged over the construction months only (no lease-up). LTC 55% = 0.38, 60% = 0.40, 65% = 0.43, 70% = 0.45, nearly independent of a 12-24 month duration. Pari-passu funding (equity and loan drawn pro rata) would give about 0.60 instead."
      }
     }
    },
    "interestReserveConvention": {
     "id": "interestReserveConvention",
     "name": "Interest reserve convention",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "",
     "range": {
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [],
       "derived": false,
       "method": ""
      }
     }
    },
    "permanentLoanRate": {
     "id": "permanentLoanRate",
     "name": "Permanent / takeout loan rate (fixed, 7-10 year)",
     "basis": "",
     "notes": "Used for stabilized-value or refinance checks, not by the construction budget. exitCapRate guidance is out of scope here (no sourced 2026 cap-rate survey retrieved).",
     "range": {
      "low": 0.065,
      "mid": 0.071,
      "high": 0.077,
      "source": {
       "file": "_common/financing.json",
       "evidence": [
        "_common/financing.json#e7",
        "_common/financing.json#e8"
       ],
       "derived": true,
       "method": "10-year Treasury about 5.0-5.3% (e7; October 2026 average 5.19%) + spread. Spreads are an assumption (no public current survey retrieved): agency multifamily / life-company ~+1.4 to +1.8; bank / CMBS ~+1.9 to +2.5. Low = 5.10+1.40 = 6.5%. Mid = 5.19+1.90 = about 7.1%. High = 5.19+2.50 = about 7.7%."
      }
     }
    }
   },
   "method": "Rates are anchored to FRED market data as of 2026-10-21/24 (SOFR, prime, Fed target, Treasuries). Lender spreads, LTC, fees and draw-balance factors are derived conventions, not survey data: the web-search budget ran out before a public spread/LTC survey (e.g. CBRE, MBA, Trepp) could be located. Verify with current term sheets. All values are decimals."
  },
